1
00:00:00,262 --> 00:00:04,612
At thirty-five thousand feet, why
put a hole in a pressurized window?

2
00:00:04,890 --> 00:00:08,615
In this Airbus design, look through
the scratch pane you can touch.

3
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:12,075
Behind it, a tiny vent
pierces the inner windowpane.

4
00:00:12,085 --> 00:00:14,460
Beyond that is the outer windowpane.

5
00:00:15,774 --> 00:00:19,514
The vent lets cabin air into the
gap between the structural panes.

6
00:00:19,524 --> 00:00:21,724
It is not a hole to the outside.

7
00:00:21,884 --> 00:00:25,349
That puts cabin pressure on
both sides of the inner pane.

8
00:00:25,359 --> 00:00:28,484
The outer pane normally carries
the pressure difference.

9
00:00:28,781 --> 00:00:32,696
If the outer windowpane fails, the
inner windowpane can take the pressure

10
00:00:32,706 --> 00:00:33,656
load.

11
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,710
The scratch pane protects
against passenger contact.

12
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:37,660
Three layers.

13
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:38,995
Different jobs.
